   <table:table table:name="Tabla1" table:style-name="Tabla1">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Tabla1.A"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Tabla1.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Tabla1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents"><text:span text:style-name="T2">About this document.</text:span> This guide documents choz 1.3.<text:span text:style-name="T1">18</text:span>. It is written for the terminal application; choz&apos;s effects and its four artifacts (arpeggiator, step sequencer, metronome and arranger) are also published as a CLAP plugin for other hosts, and choz itself runs inside a DAW as a CLAP instrument — see section 2.5.<text:line-break/>Screenshots were taken from choz running on Linux with the JACK/PipeWire backend. Device, bank and preset names in them belong to that installation and will differ on yours. </text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
