   <text:p text:style-name="Cuerpo_20_de_20_texto.cap">Figure 5.3 — A SoundFont loaded in tab 1: the BANK/PRESET row and the SF2 engine&apos;s knob box.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc2445_3455341890"/>5.3 SFZ and WAV<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc2445_3455341890"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">SFZ instruments play on choz&apos;s own 32-voice sampler and a WAV plays as a rack source; both load from the same picker. A SoundFont player installed as a plugin appears under its own format tab and is used like any other plugin.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc2447_3455341890"/>5.4 Banks and presets<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc2447_3455341890"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">2</text:span> (or <text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">b</text:span>) opens the bank and preset browser. The highlighted row sounds while you move through it, and <text:span text:style-name="T2">SELECT</text:span> keeps it. When a plugin&apos;s patches are files rather than numbered programs, the same button opens the categories its own window would show.</text:p>
