   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">l</text:span> lists the learnable targets of the active tab: volume and pan, mute and solo, bank up and down, parameter page, instrument reset, effects on and moved, add effect, the arpeggiator (on/off, tap, hold), the four sounds, the tabs, and every instrument parameter. Pick one, then move the controller. <text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">3</text:span> does it the other way round — pick the control on screen first — and the <text:span text:style-name="T2">LEARN</text:span> button lets you learn by clicking a knob.</text:p>
