   <text:p text:style-name="Cuerpo_20_de_20_texto.cap">Figure 8.3 — MIDI learn: the tab&apos;s targets, including every plugin parameter.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc2483_3455341890"/>8.4 KEYS and panic<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc2483_3455341890"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The <text:span text:style-name="T2">KEYS</text:span> panel draws the keyboard with the notes sounding, the pitch bend and the modulation wheel, one colour per tab. <text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">P</text:span> (or <text:span text:style-name="T2">F9</text:span>, or <text:span text:style-name="T2">PANIC</text:span>) silences everything left hanging.</text:p>
