   <text:p text:style-name="Cuerpo_20_de_20_texto.cap">Figure 9.2 — The sequencer: play, record, part, quantise, time signature, song chain, clear, swing, randomness and probability.</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="L2">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P14"><text:span text:style-name="T2">▶</text:span> plays the pattern from the top of the song chain, <text:span text:style-name="T2">⏸</text:span> leaves and comes back in the same part of the chain, <text:span text:style-name="T2">■</text:span> stops and rewinds. <text:span text:style-name="T2">K</text:span> in the box still toggles play and stop.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P14"><text:span text:style-name="T2">■ takes the metronome with it</text:span> when something was playing: a click over a stopped rack is a click nobody asked for. Pausing does not.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P14"><text:span text:style-name="T2">METER</text:span> opens the bar: beats, unit, grouping, and how many steps that makes. It is the session&apos;s time signature — the metronome&apos;s — because there is one bar in this program.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P15"><text:span text:style-name="T2">Steps are counted from every downbeat of that bar.</text:span> A bar that is not a whole number of steps (7/8 at quarter steps is three and a half) ends on a short step, and steps past the sixteen the grid holds are rests, so step 1 is always the metronome&apos;s one.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___TocChoz3_2026"/>9.3 Arranger<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___TocChoz3_2026"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The arranger is a backing band from a chord chart: bass, drums, piano and guitar playing a progression in a style. A tab plays one artifact at a time, so switching the arranger on (its tab switch on the <text:span text:style-name="T2">ARR</text:span> tab of the generator box) switches that tab&apos;s arpeggiator and sequencer off. Switching it on does not start it: <text:span text:style-name="T2">▶</text:span> does.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr1" draw:name="fig_arranger.png" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="16cm" svg:height="5.271cm"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
